course: dictionary
lesson: 13627
title: One, separate, or special
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word individual has a few meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one. As an adjective it means single and separate, made for one person or thing only. «Each child was given an individual cake.» Each child got their own cake, not one shared cake.
explain: As a noun, an individual is one person, thought of on their own rather than as part of a group. «The coach spoke to each individual in the team.» Clue words like each, one and separate tell you the author means one person at a time.
explain: Individual can also mean different from others and special to one person. «Her drawings have an individual style that nobody else has.» The style belongs to her alone, so it is not the same as anyone else's.
fact: Individual means single and separate, made for one person or thing only.
fact: As a noun, an individual is one person, thought of on their own.
fact: Individual work means work that each person does alone, not in a group.
fact: «Individual portions» means a separate portion for each person.
fact: Individual can also mean special to one person, so use the sentence clues to find out which meaning is right.
exercise: «Each child was given an individual cake.» What does individual mean here? | Cut into pieces for everyone | Very big and round | Left over at the end | *One for each child, not shared
exercise: Miss Patel says, «Today you will do individual work, not group work.» What does individual work mean? | Work that parents must check | Work done in a team of four | Work that is hard to finish | *Work done by each person alone
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means one person thought of on their own: «The coach spoke to each individual in the team.» | team | *individual | spoke | coach
test: In a shop, the sign says «individual price: 50p». What does individual price mean? | The price that goes up each week | The price for a group of friends | The price for the whole box | *The price of one item
test: «Her drawings have an individual style that nobody else has.» What does individual mean here? | Written in pencil | *Different from others, special to one person | Shared by everyone in the class | Single and on its own in a crowd
exam: Lila says individual always means one person. Is she right? | Yes, it always means a shared thing | No, it only ever means a group | *No, it can mean one person, one item, or something special to one person | Yes, it only ever means a person
